# Mobile app environment variables (OPTIONAL)
#
# Copy to .env.local if you need to override defaults:
#   cp .env.sample .env.local
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars into the JS bundle at build time.
# Non-public vars exist only during the build, not in the running app.
# .env.local is gitignored; .env.sample is checked in as documentation.

# Override the backend API URL. When unset, lib/env.ts auto-detects
# based on platform and environment (localhost / LAN / Vercel prod).
# Set this when auto-detection doesn't fit your setup:
#   - Backend runs on a non-default port
#   - Testing against a deployed API from a local build
#   - Network can't route from the device to Metro's advertised host
#
# Examples:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:9000
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://staging.example.com/api
#EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
